<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <name>Architecture</name>
  <type>concept:Architecture</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to the MachineBlocks layered architecture</is>

  <documentation>
    MachineBlocks follows a layered architecture:

    MBML (MachineBlocks Markup Language)
      ↓
    MBOM (MachineBlocks Object Model)
      ↓
    Render Target (reference: OpenSCAD)
      ↓
    STL / 3MF (or other target artifacts)

    MBML is the declarative authoring format for blocks, sets, and devices. Authors describe typed,
    parameterized elements without knowledge of any render target.

    MBOM is the renderer-independent canonical object model. The MBML compiler produces MBOM.
    Validation, composition, and domain semantics operate on MBOM.

    A render target serializes MBOM into a concrete output language. The MachineBlocks V3 SCAD
    library is the reference render target: OpenSCAD files that OpenSCAD turns into STL or 3MF.
    MBOM is canonical; SCAD is a serialization of MBOM — not the other way around.

    Core principle: one native geometry primitive with a large parameter space. Complexity comes
    from parameter combinations, composition of multiple blocks, and nesting — not from many
    unrelated primitives.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:UnitsAndGrid" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — unit stack, grid aspect ratio, and bounding box.
    </see>
    <see type="mbml:MbmlOverview" relation="SeeAlso">
      MBML authoring path on this architecture.
    </see>
    <see type="scad:ScadRenderTarget" relation="SeeAlso">
      OpenSCAD as the reference render target.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/03_mbom.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      MBOM specialization of BOM Core.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/05_scad_renderer.md" relation="DeepDive">
      SCAD render target registration and processors.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
